From 09cb9671e4f5b67f10421420da90570bb5784dac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:38:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - clamp the inclusive maximum
 voltage

The inclusive level formula adds a step before scaling by byte-sized
speed. At maximum speed the voltage exceeds the variant maximum. On a
legacy five-bit drive field, code 32 then wraps to zero.

Clamp the scaled voltage before encoding it, retaining the existing
inclusive distribution. Refresh Timothy Schmidt's original fix onto
the verified current input-next source.

Codex (GPT-6) assisted this port and expanded source-bound sanitizer
checks. The complete series passes 86077 checks; removing this clamp
fails 144 checks. Native ARM/ARM64 vibrator and FF-helper objects
compile with W=1 and no diagnostics. This host evidence does not
qualify a booted current-maintainer tree or physical force feedback.

Fixes: 48c0687a322d ("Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - correct VIB_MAX_LEVELS calculation")

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
index 26476a3e3837..e1d69089d4bd 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
@@ -159,6 +159,8 @@ static void pm8xxx_work_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 		vib->level = VIB_MIN_LEVEL_mV(vib);
 	}
 
+	vib->level = min(vib->level, VIB_MAX_LEVEL_mV(vib));
+
 	pm8xxx_vib_set(vib, vib->active);
 }
 
